  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "The consecutive angles of a trapezoid form an arithmetic sequence. If the smallest angle is \\(75^\\circ,\\) then the largest angle is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(95^\\circ\\)",
    "B": "\\(100^\\circ\\)",
    "C": "\\(105^\\circ\\)",
    "D": "\\(110^\\circ\\)",
    "E": "\\(115^\\circ\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "In a four-term arithmetic sequence, the first and fourth terms have the same sum as the second and third terms, because the terms are equally spaced. The first and fourth terms are also the smallest and largest, in some order.\n\nLet \\(L\\) be the largest angle measure, in degrees. A trapezoid is a quadrilateral, so its interior angles sum to \\(360^\\circ\\). Pairing the angles therefore gives\n\\[\n2(75+L)=360.\n\\]\nHence \\(75+L=180\\), so \\(\\boxed{L=105}\\). The largest angle is \\(105^\\circ\\), choice C.",
